# Vite only reads VITE_* variables.
#
# `npm run dev` uses localhost:8080 by default. Leave these commented
# unless you want the UI preview to hit a remote API.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8080/api
# VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8080/ws
#
# Extension / Chrome Web Store build (`npm run build:extension`):
# Vite loads `.env.extension` automatically because the script uses
# `--mode extension`. If that file is missing, the build falls back
# to the live Render service:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://algoarena-rc9v.onrender.com/api
#   VITE_WS_URL=wss://algoarena-rc9v.onrender.com/ws
#
# Copy those two lines into `.env.extension` only if you need to override
# the defaults. Do not put production URLs in `.env` or `npm run dev`
# will talk to Render instead of localhost.
#
# Optional TURN (helps voice across school/office NATs). Comma-separated URLs:
# VITE_TURN_URL=turn:turn.example.com:3478,turns:turn.example.com:443
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
